  "engine": "racket",
  "description": "ITF Rule 10 (Change of Ends), verified per set rather than as a match-wide continuous count: set 1 closes 6-3 (9 games, odd) -> change due at set end AND again after set 2's very first game; set 2 closes 6-4 (10 games, even) -> no extra change at set end, deferred to after set 3's first game. A continuous match-wide odd/even count would wrongly miss the change after set 2's first game.",
